 the vast majority of other  russian prisoners  to commun to communicate with the  outside world  so he is protected in some way but then  as you say he is coming  under psychological pressure he's being  woken up  every night um once an hour throughout  the night so it's certainly not that  he's getting  particularly special treatment or not  that he's being left alone  by these prison wardens well that  treatment of course is considered uh  torture by some and  how did supporters and the family of  navalny react  to this message  well we don't have any statement from  his family yet  supporters have been sharing it very  widely  on social media there's certainly the  the feeling that  any news is is not necessarily good news  but it's definitely  a relief because he's been out of  contact  for the last few days he was out of  contact before  during his jailing when he was being  transferred from one  institution to another and whenever that  happens there is a lot of anxiety about  where he is and if anything might have  happened to him  so the the reaction to this has it  certainly  calmed his supporters to a certain  extent just to know where he  is even if it is in an institution of  this kind  uh here today navalny was expected to  attend a hearing in a moscow court via  video link  uh at issue was his  lawyers um  accusation really that moscow is doing  too little to investigate navalny's  poisoning  what came out of this hearing  well the hearing's actually been  postponed until next week  it was a very brief court hearing his  lawyer was launching a complaint  launching an appeal  against the lack of investigation into  his poisoning  in siberia we actually didn't hear from  navalny at  all in the end we just heard from a  state prosecutor  who said that he didn't see any reason  for this  complaint to be upheld it's almost  certainly  not going to be upheld the authorities  aren't going to investigate  anything that they don't want to  investigate  so real